# Production API origin, read by `vite build` (mode=production).
#
# This is a BUILD-time value, not a runtime one. Vite inlines every VITE_* into
# the bundle the same way Next inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* — setting it as a runtime
# environment variable on the host does nothing, and changing it means a
# rebuild and redeploy, not a config flip.
#
# Committed rather than left to a dashboard setting so the deployed origin is
# reproducible from a clone: `npm run build` produces the same bundle anywhere.
# A hosting platform's own env var still wins over this file if one is set,
# which is what you want for a one-off preview against a different backend.
#
# Empty/unset means relative paths, which is correct for local dev (vite's proxy
# in vite.config.js forwards to 127.0.0.1:8000) and for a single-origin
# container serving both halves.
VITE_API_URL=https://helioops-production.up.railway.app
